      "text": "Robert: [58:3] ...shall expiate by freeing a slave before they resume intercourse. This is to admonish you. God is Cognizant of everything you do. [58:4] If you cannot find a slave to free, then you shall fast two consecutive months before resuming intercourse. And those unable to fast shall feed sixty poor persons. This is for you to believe in God and His messenger. These are God's laws, and the rejecters have deserved painful retribution. [58:5] Those who oppose God and His messenger are doomed like those before them who were doomed. We have revealed clear revelations, and the disbelievers therein have deserved painful retribution. [58:6] The day will come when God resurrects them, then informs them of everything they had done. God has recorded it while they forgot. God witnesses all things. [58:7] Do you not realize that God knows everything in the heavens and the earth? No three people can meet in secrecy without Him being the fourth, nor five without Him being the sixth, nor less than this, nor more, without Him being there. Then, on the Day of Resurrection, He will inform them of everything they did. God is fully aware of all things. [58:8] Those who are prohibited from conspiracy, then go back to it, conspiring sinfully, maliciously, and in defiance of the messenger. When they come to you, they greet you not with God's greetings, and say to themselves, let us see if God will punish us for what we say. Their only destiny is Hell wherein they burn; what a miserable destiny. [58:9] O you who believe, if you have to confer secretly, you shall not confer to commit sin, transgression, and disobedience to the messenger. You may confer only to work righteousness and piety. Beware of God, for you will be gathered before Him. All right, we'll stop there. All right, verse one. [58:1] God has heard the woman who debated with you about her husband and complained to God... [58:2] Those among you who estranged their wives as if they were their mothers are doing wrong... Obviously, this is in the Quran for a reason. God...",
